boats are killing cute fuzzy^H^H^H^H^Hrubbery dolphins.  Of course when he's 
on one boat, the other boats go back to biz as usual.)  In cases like this,
I see 2 things at work when the enviros *I* know advocate having the govt.
crack down on something like this:
1) they are sick of the lipservice and hypocrisy they get from the govt. If the
govt says it will do something, it should do it and do it RIGHT.
2) if they can USE the govt to get what they want, without giving them anymore
power than they already have, go for it. This is called "milking the system".

I think 1) is right on target, as long as one is also trying to get the govt
to say it will do fewer things that it has no biz doing.  It is an outrage
against govt. dishonesty, nothing more nothing less.  And I think 2) is rather
dangerous.  That is basically how shit like the privacy clipper get started,
and snowball out of control.

Just some opinions.  But in general, based on MY experience, I find the 
characterization of environmentalists as govt lovers who think the people
can't possibly control themselves and the govt has to do it for them, is
really quite silly.  How can a movement (more accurately, a bunch of dis-
parate movements with a few things in common), that shows anti-govt prop-
aganda films, that is mostly (in my experience!) made up of neo-hippies
(and plenty of the originals), anarchists, and other people general opposed
to govt., be IN FAVOUR of the govt?  It just doesn't add up in my estimation.
